{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/992672-dragonblooded-mutants-and-beastmen","id":992672,"title":"Dragonblooded mutants and beastmen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-24T18:46:21-07:00","id":992672,"title":"Dragonblooded mutants and beastmen","content":"My understanding is that by the time of the setting the blood of the dragons had spread to every corner of the world. Between that and the fact that the Realm has been enslaving beastmen for a long time, chances are good that there are beastmen and women who draw the second breath as one of the terrestrials. Given the general prejudice against the descendants of the lunar anathema by the the followers of the Immaculate philosophy, how would a fire aspected wolfman or a wood aspected catgirl be treated by The Realm as a whole and the individual houses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12550-oglantash","name":"OGLantash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T19:07:04-07:00","id":992686,"title":"","content":"Very interesting, I imagine a lot of racism. They likely will be Lost Eggs rather then Adopted into a House if they don't force them to join the Cloister so they don't taint the gene pool of the isle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T19:10:51-07:00","id":992689,"title":"","content":"Well, it depends on how animalistic the beastman is.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind though that the Realm Dragon Blooded tend to look down on Outcaste Dragon Blooded who were born in the the Threshold and treat them as lessers. I imagine even the nicest and most progressive Houses would treat a beastman Dragon Blooded like a third-class Dragon Blooded <i>at best</i>. Such a Dragon Blooded would be viewed as a symbol of shame and would probably face severe social pressure to stay out of the public spotlight as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Ultimately such an individual would be considered &quot;someone who shouldn't allowed to exist.&quot; They have the blessings of the Dragons so they can't be killed or ignored out of hand, but at the same time I don't think the powers of the Realm accept such a person. They would likely be given assigned to the Legions and posted in bumfuck nowehere or else assigned to the Wyld Hunt and basically sent off to die for the good the Creation.<br /> <br /> Such a Dragon Blooded, of course, could make individual friends and allies. But I think ultimately he or she would always face a life of fairly severe discrimination and be looked down on with scorn not just by the Dragon Blooded born in the Realm, but even other Outcastes who themeselves often face discrimination from other Dragon Blooded. <br /> <br /> Now, if we're talking a cute anime cat girl or fox girl, I imagine they would still face discrimination, but maybe not the same kind that an Elkman or Wolfman would face. Still being viewed as sexually desirable due to fetishistic features can be just as bad or even worse as the discrimination faced by more inhuman looking creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T19:19:52-07:00","id":992692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/992672-dragonblooded-mutants-and-beastmen?p=992689#post992689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it depends on how animalistic the beastman is.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind though that the Realm Dragon Blooded tend to look down on Outcaste Dragon Blooded who were born in the the Threshold and treat them as lessers. I imagine even the nicest and most progressive Houses would treat a beastman Dragon Blooded like a third-class Dragon Blooded <i>at best</i>. Such a Dragon Blooded would be viewed as a symbol of shame and would probably face severe social pressure to stay out of the public spotlight as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Ultimately such an individual would be considered &quot;someone who shouldn't allowed to exist.&quot; They have the blessings of the Dragons so they can't be killed or ignored out of hand, but at the same time I don't think the powers of the Realm accept such a person. They would likely be given assigned to the Legions and posted in bumfuck nowehere or else assigned to the Wyld Hunt and basically sent off to die for the good the Creation.<br /> <br /> Such a Dragon Blooded, of course, could make individual friends and allies. But I think ultimately he or she would always face a life of fairly severe discrimination and be looked down on with scorn not just by the Dragon Blooded born in the Realm, but even other Outcastes who themeselves often face discrimination from other Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> Now, if we're talking a cute anime cat girl or fox girl, I imagine they would still face discrimination, but maybe not the same kind that an Elkman or Wolfman would face. Still being viewed as sexually desirable due to fetishistic features can be just as bad or even worse as the discrimination faced by more inhuman looking creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be particularly interesting if the beastgirl was born and raised on the Blessed Isle. You know there is at least one Cynis who keeps a menagerie and does things with his pets the immaculate priests would frown on. I can imagine the owner/father of such a terrestrial finding themselves with the oddest mix of pride and shame at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12550-oglantash","name":"OGLantash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T19:31:30-07:00","id":992695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OGLantash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/992672-dragonblooded-mutants-and-beastmen#post992672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that by the time of the setting the blood of the dragons had spread to every corner of the world. Between that and the fact that the Realm has been enslaving beastmen for a long time, chances are good that there are beastmen and women who draw the second breath as one of the terrestrials. <b>Given the general prejudice against the descendants of the lunar anathema</b> by the the followers of the Immaculate philosophy, how would a fire aspected wolfman or a wood aspected catgirl be treated by The Realm as a whole and the individual houses?</div> </div> </div> </div>They might actually be mostly Wyld mutants in this edition. Some beastfolk might still have Lunar origins, but an awful lot won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T19:33:41-07:00","id":992697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/992672-dragonblooded-mutants-and-beastmen?p=992695#post992695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They might actually be mostly Wyld mutants in this edition. Some beastfolk might still have Lunar origins, but an awful lot won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, but either way it makes little difference, the Dynasts are no keener on wyld mutants than they are on lunar spawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12550-oglantash","name":"OGLantash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T19:39:52-07:00","id":992702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OGLantash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/992672-dragonblooded-mutants-and-beastmen?p=992692#post992692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know there is at least one Cynis who keeps a menagerie and does things with his pets the immaculate priests would frown on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless there's a specific canon character you have in mind - that I'm simply forgetting about - I <i>don't</i> know that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T20:04:37-07:00","id":992717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OGLantash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/992672-dragonblooded-mutants-and-beastmen?p=992692#post992692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be particularly interesting if the beastgirl was born and raised on the Blessed Isle. You know there is at least one Cynis who keeps a menagerie and does things with his pets the immaculate priests would frown on. I can imagine the owner/father of such a terrestrial finding themselves with the oddest mix of pride and shame at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>And to think I had almost forgotten about Cynis Goatfucker from page 97 of Aspect Book: Wood, though to be fair he was never one of my favorite characters. Still, I'm not certain that he is still going to be considered canon in 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T20:08:18-07:00","id":992719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/992672-dragonblooded-mutants-and-beastmen?p=992702#post992702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless there's a specific canon character you have in mind - that I'm simply forgetting about - I <i>don't</i> know that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would not put it past Sesus Nagazzar, Cynis Anbor, Ragara Bhagwei, Ledaal Kes, Cynis Belar, or The Scarlet Empress herself. But no, I do not have any proof that any of them diddled with their menageries. That being said, with over 10,000 potential dragonblooded slave owners, there is room for all sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12550,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12550-oglantash","user":"OGLantash","date":".  Forgot Cynis Anbor 10-24-2016, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12550-oglantash","name":"OGLantash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T21:55:09-07:00","id":992767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OGLantash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/992672-dragonblooded-mutants-and-beastmen?p=992719#post992719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I would not put it past Sesus Nagazzar\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a Cynis. Besides, he's got his twins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OGLantash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/992672-dragonblooded-mutants-and-beastmen?p=992719#post992719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ragara Bhagwei\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a Cynis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OGLantash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/992672-dragonblooded-mutants-and-beastmen?p=992719#post992719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ledaal Kes\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a Cynis. Also, <i>you</i> may not put it past him, but I would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OGLantash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/992672-dragonblooded-mutants-and-beastmen?p=992719#post992719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026or The Scarlet Empress herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mothered Cynis, but not Cynis herself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T22:38:59-07:00","id":993330,"title":"","content":"Ledaal Kes is gay. So, that fact alone means he's unlikely to have beastmen kids.<br /> <br /> That said, I hope that the Realm book goes into this a bit. I'd like a bit of explicit text about it.<br /> <br /> I also have to wonder if the reason you have cat ears matters at all. I mean, I'd assume that if one of your parents was the god of cats, a Lunar, a cat beastman, or just was out in the Wyld a bunch, each of those different backgrounds would have a different effect on your life and social standing, but it's also not necessarily obvious which of those back stories is correct.<br /> <br /> I feel like claiming one of your parents was a god is probably the best out of a number of bad options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 10-26-2016, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T23:19:32-07:00","id":993346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OGLantash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/992672-dragonblooded-mutants-and-beastmen#post992672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that by the time of the setting the blood of the dragons had spread to every corner of the world. Between that and the fact that the Realm has been enslaving beastmen for a long time, chances are good that there are beastmen and women who draw the second breath as one of the terrestrials. Given the general prejudice against the descendants of the lunar anathema by the the followers of the Immaculate philosophy, how would a fire aspected wolfman or a wood aspected catgirl be treated by The Realm as a whole and the individual houses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dependent at least somewhat on the Beastman Terrestrial's behvaior, it'd either be seen as the manifest will of the Dragons, or Anathema trickery.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}